-42f6-94e1-6b581739cfdf", "title": "Italy's workplace-deaths epidemic continues as man falls down lift shaft", "url": "https://www.ansa.it/english/news/general_news/2026/09/24/italys-workplace-deaths-epidemic-continues-as-man-falls-down-lift-shaft_9beafecb-e10e-4806-b3c1-9f7c6db823f6.html", "summary": "(ANSA) - ROME, 24 SET - Italy's workplace-deaths epidemic continued late on Wednesday when the body of a 51-year-old Albanian man was found at a building where a renovation is under way.\nThe man, the owner of a Vicenza-based company specializing in masonry, is believed to have died of injuries caused by him falling down an elevator shaft.\nHis body was found after his family raised the alarm when he failed to return home.\nThe Colosseum in Rome, meanwhile, will remain closed to the public on Thursday after Andrea Moretti, a 22-year-old rope-access worker, died on the night between Tuesday and Wednesday in a fall while installing a new lighting system.\nThe monument was also closed on Wednesday.\nOn Tuesday workplace accident insurance agency INAIL said in its annual report that Italy registered 1,189 work-related deaths in 2025.\nAlthough this was 37 fewer than in 2024, a drop of 3.02%, it still means that Italy is averaging over three work-related deaths every day. (ANSA).Read article...", "published_at": "2026-09-24T09:04:37+00:00", "image_url": "https://www.ansa.it/webimages/img_1280x720/2026/9/24/04e2a621da2d3c493556cbc15d291bbb.jpg", "source": {"name": "ANSA (English)", "tier": "international", "url": "https://www.ansa.it/english/"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 50, "sensationalism": 15, "opinion_fact": 14, "factual_rigor": 31, "framing": 10, "confidence": 0.45, "rationale": {"lean": {"keyword_score": 50.0, "framing_shift": 0.0, "entity_shift": 0.0, "sentence_direction": 0.0, "text_score": 50.0, "source_baseline": 50, "text_shift": 0.0, "delta_max": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "top_left_keywords": [], "top_right_keywords": [], "framing_phrases_found": [], "enti